From: Uke Linux project <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Notify service readiness after registering the FastRPC listener

Start the sensor PD only after the root listener has registered, and publish
SensorProxy only after the sensor listener has registered. Exec completion
does not establish either protocol boundary.

--- a/hexagonrpcd/rpcd.c
+++ b/hexagonrpcd/rpcd.c
@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@
 #include "listener.h"
 #include "localctl.h"
 #include "rpcd_builder.h"
+#include <systemd/sd-daemon.h>
 
 static int register_fastrpc_listener(int fd)
 {
@@ -219,6 +220,8 @@
 	if (ret)
 		goto err;
 
+	sd_notify(0, "READY=1");
+
 	run_fastrpc_listener(fd, n_ifaces, ifaces);
 
 	fastrpc_localctl_deinit(ifaces[REMOTECTL]);
